  303: class LLMProviderRegistry:
  304:     """Owns the canonical list of LLM providers.
  305: 
  306:     Construct once per backend process. Pass ``config.toml`` path. The
  307:     constructor loads existing ``[[llm.endpoints]]`` entries from disk;
  308:     if absent, the registry starts empty.
  309: 
  310:     Concurrency: mutating methods (``add_provider``, ``remove_provider``,
  311:     ``set_enabled``, ``reorder``, ``update_provider``) are async to leave
  312:     room for a ws broadcast in Phase 2. Within a single backend process
  313:     the ws handler serializes ``settings_providers_*`` messages, so we
