    1: # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 DennyWanye
    2: # SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1
    3: 
    4: """LLMProviderRegistry 鈥?P5-S2 Phase 1 (multi-provider-management).
    5: 
    6: This is the single source of truth for the user's list of LLM providers.
    7: Owns:
    8:   - In-memory list of ProviderEntry dataclasses
    9:   - Atomic persistence to `config.toml` `[[llm.endpoints]]` array
   10:   - API keys stored in OS keychain under service "deskpet", account
   11:     "provider.<provider_id>" (NEVER plaintext in toml)
   12:   - Migration of legacy `[llm.local]` single-provider schema 鈫?new list
   13: 
   14: Schema in config.toml::
   15: 
   16:     [[llm.endpoints]]
   17:     id = "relay-deepseek"
   18:     name = "Relay DeepSeek"
   19:     base_url = "https://api.your-llm-relay.example.com/v1"
   20:     model = "deepseek-v3"
   21:     api_key_ref = "deskpet.provider.relay-deepseek"
   22:     priority = 1
   23:     enabled = true
   24: 
   25: `api_key_ref` is the only secret-shaped field. The real key lives in the
   26: OS keychain at `keyring.get_password("deskpet", "provider.<id>")`. The
   27: ``api_key_ref`` string is just a UI hint; persistence is keyed by ``id``.
   28: 
   29: Public API::
   30: 
   31:     reg = LLMProviderRegistry(path_to_config_toml)
   32:     await reg.add_provider({...})
   33:     reg.list_providers()                # api_key redacted to "********"
   34:     reg.get_chain()                     # enabled, ordered by priority
   35:     await reg.remove_provider(id)
   36:     await reg.set_enabled(id, enabled)
   37:     await reg.reorder([id1, id2, ...])
   38:     await reg.update_provider(id, **patch)
   39: 
   40: All mutating methods are async because Phase 2 will broadcast a
   41: ``providers_changed`` ws event; for Phase 1 we just keep the signature
   42: shape so chat-handler can await without refactor later.
   43: 
   44: Migration: ``_migrate_legacy_provider_config(path)`` is a free function so
   45: ``main.py`` lifespan can call it before constructing the registry.

